[#:seon.task{:name "agents-can-validate"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "An agent can validate a value against a registered schema key from its SCI context in one ordinary call. Historical: passed on branch exp-validate-2 from the brief alone, never delivered; that branch is not retained."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/valid-candidate-value? seon.schema/explain-candidate-value seon.schema/projection-from-database}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/experiments/tasks-v02/seon.schema.edn"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/language-requirements-2026-09-24.md"
                         "docs/prds/agent-platform/landing/lane-impl-task-slice2-2026-09-25.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "validation-throws-on-non-keyword-sorted-maps"
             :kind :function
             :intent "valid-candidate-value? throws ClassCastException (Keyword.compareTo) on a sorted map with symbol or string keys, because Malli's map validation calls get with a keyword on it. At the agent REPL the throw escapes settlement: the run never closes and every later form answers agent-already-running until the branch is retired (maintainer #5; analyst probe 5 timed out at 60,258 ms). Symbol- and String-to-Keyword casts in seon.cluster.agent/turn-step were recorded as core faults at 16:02-16:10Z. Validate without a keyword lookup on foreign sorted maps, and settle any throw as the run's failure."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/valid-candidate-value?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-dogfood-analyst-astra-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-maintainer-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/stability-guard-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/armed-error-validation-throws-on-non-keyword-sorted-maps.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "register-works-only-top-level"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.schema/register! inside let or any nested form refuses 'Schema declarations require an isolated registration delta' (schema.clj:1279): the delta opens only for a syntactically top-level register!. The first run of three register! took 1,786 ms and eight took 3,681 ms. Open the delta around any register! reached during a form."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/begin-registration-delta seon.schema/register!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/schema-registration-works-only-as-a-top-level-form.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-projection-travels-ambiently"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The projection still travels in dynamic Vars (*projection*, *projection-state*, *packaged-forms*, *candidate-forms-overlay*) plus a registration-delta candidate atom: 18 handed-projection, 42 call-with-projection (16 files), 12 call-with-projection-state and 5 call-with-forms call sites. db/carried-projection already answers the same value in 0.01 ms. The current JVM's profile shows call-with-projection-state inclusive 229,243 ms, max 55,673 ms, x97, which also hides real costs from profiles. Convert readers to the carried projection and delete the ambient Vars (C5); C2 waits on this."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.schema/call-with-projection seon.schema/call-with-projection-state seon.schema/handed-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/delete-r8-r6-r10-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-declaration-write-reloads-the-whole-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every declaration-touching write (a new function, a spec or schema change) pays load-projection from an identical base: 35-42 ms, O(program) even when nothing else differs. Derive the projection incrementally from the changed declarations."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.schema/load-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-write-cost-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "canonical-definition-cannot-invert-evaluated-roots"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A refusal of any contract holding [:fn ns/pred] armed from Var metadata cannot be built: canonicalization tries to invert compiled predicates. Model fix (Astra M3): preserve the admitted declarative form at arming; never canonicalize a compiled schema while building a refusal."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/canonical-definition seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/agent-path-2-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "map-validation-throws-on-sorted-maps-with-foreign-keys"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Malli's :map validator looks each declared key up (malli core.cljc:1276); a sorted map whose comparator cannot compare that key with its own keys throws ClassCastException instead of answering false (fault fa60ad84, seon.schema/valid-candidate-value? from turn-step, 17:13Z). The producer site was fixed in seon.turn/disposition (f83931226) by validating only maps that name the discriminator, and seon.render.value/keyword-lookup? guards the same class in render: two copies of one guard. Validating an arbitrary value against a candidate schema belongs to one owner; decide there, once, so callers delete their guards."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/valid-candidate-value? seon.turn/disposition seon.render.value/keyword-lookup?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-boot-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-function-contract-changes-the-schema-projection"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Function contract entities are a projection range (seon.schema/projection-ranges :function-contract-rows), so every contracted defn makes a new projection value: load-projection (36-50 ms, ~94 MB) and every projection-keyed derivation re-walks ~3,550 forms. Measured 2026-09-26 on pid 89341: (defn f [x] (inc x)) 134 ms, 157 MB, 26k armed calls; the same defn with {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} 757 ms, 1.21 GB, 190k armed calls. Root ruling 2026-09-27: contracts leave the projection; design in docs/research/agent-platform/contracts-out-of-projection-design-2026-09-27.md."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/projection-ranges seon.schema/build-projection seon.db/carried-projection}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/defn-scan-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/contracts-out-of-projection-design-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "pull-selector-predicate-compiles-per-check"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.schema/pull-selector? compiles its whole argument (Datahike compile-pull-plan) on every armed :seon.schema/pull-selector check: 0.69 ms for the 15,060-node root selector, ten checks per walk since 18ce1b1a4 armed vector-pull and physical-selector (sci.eval-test public-walk counted 10 compiles for one plan, E6). projection-with-pulled-form-in's hit costs 2.9-3.1 ms digesting its key. Parse once per selector value (a content-keyed cache kind) or check structure only."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/pull-selector? seon.schema/projection-with-pulled-form-in}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-r6-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "schema-registration-rechecks-the-whole-program-per-key"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Registering schema keys in an evaluation costs about 300 ms per key of whole-program work, measured 2026-09-28 on default's branches through seon.schema/register! in SCI: 3 keys 951 ms (106,692 armed calls), 10 keys 2,661-2,974 ms (319,316-354,837 calls), 13 keys 3,884 ms (461,456 calls). The calls are seon.schema/contract-references (11,256 to 48,672 calls, 824 to 3,372 ms), structural-schema, compilable-form and widen-component-children: every registration re-derives the references of every contract rather than those naming the registered keys. Done when a registration's cost follows the keys it registers and the contracts that reference them (one key under 100 ms on default), with the timing in the reply."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register! seon.schema/contract-references}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/health-recording-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-check-on-three-files-exceeds-one-second",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "Review static check of seon.print, seon.render.value and value-test against packaged resources at 0daf87818 took 1301.291 ms after external JVM replacement; earlier same-class checks took 168.540 and 222.844 ms. Measure which installed contract-check operations repeat and preserve correctness; no causal ranking yet. Required full-tree clj-kondo --cache false on the archive also took 10739 ms over 494 files (0 errors/1488 warnings); that run is explicitly requested review work proportional to the whole tree, not an ordinary print. Record gate acquisition separately from warm execution; do not turn a timing observation into a wall-clock regression test.",
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-codex-notes.md"}}]
